WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.980
- [Reporter] Disney has canceled a plan

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:06.240
to build a nearly $900 million
corporate campus in Florida.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.360
It's also shutting down a
costly new hotel nearby,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.970
amid a high-profile
dispute with the governor.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.910
- The days of putting
one company on a pedestal

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.210
with no accountability are
over in the state of Florida.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.277
- [Reporter] Jacob Passy
has been covering this story

00:00:20.277 --> 00:00:23.760
for the journal and explains
why Disney is reversing course

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.133
on two of its major investments.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.960
- Disney was planning to
create an office campus

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.980
in Lake Nona, Florida, located in Orlando,

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.010
roughly 20 miles from the
Walt Disney World Resort.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.040
The campus was gonna house
roughly 2000 employees,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.390
most of whom were being relocated
from Southern California

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.150
and the campus was gonna be
about 2 million square feet,

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:51.540
so multiple buildings, and it
was a really huge development,

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.910
both for Disney and for Florida.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.550
Additionally, Star Wars:
Galactic Starcruiser

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.880
is gonna be shutting down
at the end of September.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.580
Dubbed by fans, "The Star Wars Hotel,"

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:06.090
this was a multi-day,
multi-night experience

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:09.900
where you got to live out
your own Star Wars Adventure.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.070
It was first announced back

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.460
in 2017 and opened just last March

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.050
and cost around $350 million to build,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.650
according to sources The Journal spoke to.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.480
The Galactic Starcruiser experience

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.280
came up against multiple headwinds.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.310
For starters, it was very
expensive to operate.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:33.120
Unlike a normal hotel, it
had way more employees,

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.100
folks in costumes, in
characters, roaming at all times.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.440
It was only about a hundred rooms, though.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.220
So Disney had tight
margins on this project.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.820
Disney cited changing economic
and business conditions

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.910
as their reasoning behind
shutting down these two projects.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.860
More recently, Disney has announced

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.180
that they're gonna be cutting

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.940
around 7,000 jobs across the company

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.770
and shedding around $5.5
billion in expenses.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:05.160
Disney is also in the
midst of a war of words

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.490
and a legal battle with Governor
Ron DeSantis of Florida.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:12.870
This conflict started last
year when Disney spoke out

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.420
against the so-called "Don't Say Gay Bill"

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.536
that Governor Ron DeSantis championed.

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:18.480
(crowd members applaud)

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.150
- My job is not to kowtow

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.210
to some woke corporation
in Burbank, California.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.030
My job's to stand up for
the children of my state.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:30.330
- Since then, he has championed a number

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.310
of legislative moves aimed

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:35.850
at the Reedy Creek development,
which used to control

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:39.300
the land where Walt Disney
World Resort is located.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.720
He shifted that and put in
his own political appointees

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.510
into a new board that
oversees that development.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.140
- The corporate kingdom
finally came to an end.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:48.973
(crowd cheer)

00:02:48.973 --> 00:02:50.250
- [Jacob] In response to the changes

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.930
of the Reedy Creek district,

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:54.480
Disney has filed a federal lawsuit,

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.270
claiming that DeSantis and
other Florida lawmakers

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:00.038
are retaliating against the company

00:03:00.038 --> 00:03:02.790
for exercising its First Amendment rights.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.880
- I don't think the suit has
merit, I think it's political.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.280
- These projects, were gonna
bring some high-paying jobs

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.630
to Central Florida.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:10.950
Employees there were gonna be earning,

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.890
on average, $120,000 a year.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:17.010
So you can imagine the
impact to local tax revenues

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.040
and local businesses that
were going to benefit

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:23.684
from those workers being
relocated to Florida.

00:03:23.684 --> 00:03:24.720
- [Crowd Member] Mr. Iger.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.720
- Disney CEO, Robert Iger
had previously committed

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.720
to investing $17 billion in
Florida over the next decade,

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.220
bringing thousands of jobs to the state.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.350
But right now, given these changes,

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.034
it remains to be seen whether
that actually happens.

00:03:40.034 --> 00:03:42.617
(bright music)

